 New regression assertions cover the default semantic zoom band, a 130 px minimum default Object screen width, and a maximum 3.2 layout aspect ratio across all four fixtures. The measured wrapped layouts were Small `2480 × 1258`, Medium `4338 × 2945`, Large `9333 × 3580`, and Complex `7385 × 4789`; all existing non-overlap, orthogonality, obstacle, label-point, determinism and incremental-stability checks continued to pass.
 
-## Provisional parameter adjustments
+## 2026-08-31 multi-select union impact
+
+Selection now accepts several objects at once, and the impact read model generalizes from one subject to a set:
+
+- **Selection surface.** React Flow native multi-selection is enabled: marquee/box drag on empty canvas (left button), modifier-click (Shift/Ctrl/Cmd) to add or remove, plain click unchanged. Panning moves to right/middle-button drag; wheel zoom, Controls and Minimap are unchanged. Region nodes are pointer-transparent so canvas drags start anywhere, not only between Region rectangles. Selection changes are routed through node `select` changes in `onNodesChange` — subscribing to `onSelectionChange` instead fights the controlled nodes replacement and crash-loops (update-depth exceeded; verified in-browser).
+- **Union impact.** `deriveImpact` takes the selected set: upstream is every direct dependency of any selected object, downstream every direct dependent; relationships between two selected objects are selection structure, not impact; selected objects never appear in their own impact sets. Single-select semantics (including bidirectional both-ways counting) are the `subjectIds.length === 1` case and are unchanged.
+- **Shared impact.** The impact view tracks which selected objects reach each impacted object; objects reached by more than one are marked `shared` with a `⇄ Shared N×` chip (weight variant of the same accent) and listed first in the Inspector.
+- **Aggregate Inspector.** A multi-selection binds a `kind: "objects"` Inspector: selection count, upstream/downstream/shared counts, and object lists whose entries lead to single-object inspection. Empty selection returns the Inspector to its idle state and the canvas to Browse.
+- **Line grammar.** Following project correction `corr_canvas_impact_grammar`, impact emphasis uses one established accent: edge weight plus emphasis states, direction carried by arrowheads and glyphs (↑/↓/⇄), shared marking by border weight — no per-direction hue, no glow. The earlier blue/amber direction hues were removed.
+- **Regression scope.** Focus two-hop grammar and the Trace lens are untouched; a multi-selection in Trace keeps the lens. The Fit camera frames the union of selected objects plus direct neighbors under the same per-mode zoom contract. Human Web stays read-only; the Semantic Graph, adapter, validation and layout cache are untouched.
+
+Evidence: `tests/canvas-engine.test.mjs` ("multi-object selection computes the union of impact with shared impact", including a production-registry adapter graph), and real-browser screenshots `evidence/01–07` on Small 15/20 and Medium 40/70 with 27/27 DOM checks (see `run-evidence/multiselect-browser-check.mjs`).
+
+
 
